                                Driving conditions across the UAE place rigorous demands on automotive tyres. High summer road surface temperatures accelerate rubber oxidation, hardening tread compounds and leading to premature sidewall weathering. Under UAE standard guidelines and annual RTA roadworthiness vehicle inspections, tyre age is strictly evaluated. Tyres older than five years from their DOT manufacturing date (stamped as a 4-digit code on the sidewall, showing production week and year) generally fail testing and should be replaced regardless of tread depth. While the legal minimum tread depth across the UAE is 1.6 mm, automotive safety specialists recommend considering replacement when tread wears down to 2.5 mm to 3.0 mm for dependable wet-grip and high-speed braking stability.
